      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T15:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since all fields in this struct are public. The users can modify any field after ctor. Do we really need to verify them? If it is needed, where should we put the validation code? Os just adding some assert in ctor?\n\nAlso dawn allows using different compatible view formats for single planar textures as well for core mode. For example `wgpu::TextureFormat::BGRA8Unorm` and `wgpu::TextureFormat::BGRA8UnormSrgb`. But it is not allowed with compatible mode.",
